Collision with car: Cyclist is hurled on road
While crossing the road, an 82-year-old cyclist was captured by a car and seriously injured on Wednesday in Garath.
According to the police, the 82-year-old Langenfelder had been riding his bicycle on the cycle path of the road Schwarzer Weg coming from Hilden at 12.20 a.m.
The senior wanted to cross the road at the Am Buchholler Busch road.
A passenger car driver driving in the same direction gave him priority.
When Langenfelder drove onto the road, however, he apparently did not pay attention to oncoming traffic.
He collided with a car steered by a 66-year-old Hilden woman.
The man was hurled into the street.
He suffered serious injuries and was taken to a hospital with an ambulance.
FC Bayern Munich have to do without David Alaba and Thiago in the Supercup against Borussia Dortmund
The Supercup takes place without him: David Alaba has to skip the game against Dortmund.
With personnel worries, FC Bayern travels to Dortmund for the first mandatory game of the new season.
Seven professionals are missing the defending champion in the Supercup against the cup winner.
Personnel concerns at the German football record champion Bayern Munich are getting bigger and bigger ahead of the Supercup on Saturday (20.30/ZDF and Eurosport) at cup winner Borussia Dortmund.
Coach Carlo Ancelotti also has to do without David Alaba in a duel with BVB.
This was confirmed by the Italian on Friday.
In addition, Munich's Manuel Neuer, James, Thiago, Jerome Boateng, Arjen Robben and Juan Bernat are missing.
Ancelotti has blamed the physical condition and the lack of balance in his team's five defeats in the past six Test matches.
"We know we're not in the best physical condition," Ancelotti said, adding: "The most important point is the balance in the team.
It wasn’t good last.”
However, the 58-year-old believes in an increase in performance in the first official mandatory game of the season.
"Football is also tactics, strategy, personality and motivation.
I have great confidence that my squad is showing these qualities.
The crew is ready.
We want to play intelligently," said Ancelotti, who expects a "difficult, intense game."
The duel of the two German football heavyweights captivates the fans.
The game is sold out with 81,360 spectators, the German Football League (DFL) announced on Friday.
Migrate from star to star in resin
In the resin, the first "star path" is to be created nationwide.
This is planned by the association Sternwarte Sankt Andreasberg.
There has been a planetary path in Göttingen - since 2003.
A "star path" meets the need for information of many resin visitors, it said.
It combines nature, science, exercise and sporting performance.
The members want to set up panels along the planned route and provide information about stars and constellations.
In a first phase until 2018, the association is planning "well-reachable installations at five to six locations" in the Upper Harz.
St. Andreasberg, Braunlage, Hohegeiß and Sieber would be eligible.
The information on the panels is to be supplemented via the Internet.
Therefore, a good mobile network reception plays a role in site selection.
Accessibility is also a criterion.
Later, the star path train is to be extended by train.
"On the star path, the viewers learn a lot worth knowing, for example about the physics of the individual stars," the association explained.
In addition, they learned why stars had different colors or why one star glows more strongly than another, even though it was much further afield.
It is also determined in which constellation a selected star is located and when it is best seen.
The association has been operating the highest observatory in northern Germany since 2014 in the mountain town of St. Andreasberg.
According to the Federal Office for Nature Conservation, the site in the middle of the Harz National Park is one of the six darkest regions in Germany.
Often from there the Milky Way and even the Andromeda galaxy can be clearly seen with the naked eye.
In the university city there has been something similar to the planned Sternenwerg - the Planet Trail - on the initiative of the Förderverein Planetarium Göttingen since 2003.
Beginning before Gebhard's hotel in Goetheallee, which forms the interior of our solar system, the planetary path with its steles leads up to Hainberg and the observatory - as well as an "alien" location in Diemarden (community Gleichen) with the planet Sedna.
The steles with the individual planets - including the dwarf planet-degraded Pluto at the end point - are placed exactly at a distance and scale of one to two billion.
The earth thus shrinks to a sphere of 6.5 millimeters in diameter, while the sun standing exactly 75 meters measures 70 centimeters.
The entire distance of the planetary path is a good four kilometers.
While the light from sun to Pluto takes about eight hours, pedestrians need a good hour to stele with Pluto.
Pedestrians are faster than the light in space.
However, the march to the next fixed star would last another six months.
Mikey Garcia and Vasyl Lomachenko meet for the first time discussing a possible showdown
Vasyl Lomachenko and Mikey Garcia, who were supposed to be in a litigation course to stage the most exciting boxing fight below 147 pounds in the near future, met for the first time on Thursday.
They were in separate rooms at ESPN offices in Los Angeles until Garcia, the unbeaten World Boxing Council light-weight champion, went down the hallway to greet Lomachenko, the world boxing organisation super featherweight champion.
After Garcia's victory by a unanimous decision on former four-division world champion Adrien Broner on Showtime, both fighters are members of the top-five pound-for-pound list.
Garcia stretched out his right hand and said, "How are you, champion?
I wish you the best of luck."
Lomachenko defends his belt against Miguel Marriaga at 7 p.m. on ESPN on Saturday night.
