Whelever they're ready ... "
Garcia said he appreciated Lomachenko as "an enormous fighter," and he will possibly take part in his Saturday fight.
But Lomachenko stopped at the generous praise for Garcia and said that he thought the three-fight champion from Riverside looked "very slow, I'm sorry Mikey ... you wanted the co-off".
Garcia said the focus was to show batting strength, then boxing.
Both said they could sense the momentum that was built up for their own struggle.
“This is the fight that needs to be carried out.
No other struggle creates so much attention and enthusiasm.
I'm more than happy to work on," Garcia said.
Lomachenko said: "I've been waiting for the top fighters, and that's Mikey.
It's going to be a great fight.'
Four injured after puncture
In an accident on the A7, four people were partially seriously injured on Thursday afternoon.
According to initial information, the driver of an Opel Zafira probably lost control of his vehicle shortly in front of the Marktbreit junction at about 16.30 p.m.
The car hurled to the right into the embankment, where it overturned and then remained on the roof in the green strip.
The four inmates - two adults and two children - were partially seriously injured in the accident.
During the initial care of the injured by the rescue service, the A7 to the north was closed for about an hour, then the traffic on the left lane could be routed past the accident scene.
